<title>BRAZIL: Brazil '96 exports seen about 3.0 pct up on '95.</title>
<headline>Brazil '96 exports seen about 3.0 pct up on '95.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Ministry of Industry and Commerce expects total exports for 1996 to be close to 3.0 percent higher than 1995's $46.506 billion, a senior trade official said.</p>
<p>Helio Mauro Franca, director of the ministry's department of foreign trade policy, acknowledged the growth rate was below that of other countries since the World Trade Organization was set up but said the growth in exports was a clear trend.</p>
<p>&quot;Exports in 1996 grew close to 3.0 percent (over 1995),&quot; Franca said.</p>
</text>
